A||||17||fiero56||I can't believe it||||9||
Z||000000||fiero56||11-06-2000||11:07 AM||||Few weeks ago, I bought a non-running '86 SE v-6 4-speed with just over 100k miles. Gave it a tune up, replaced fuel pump, etc, and I had it runnning perfectly.<P>I was going to take the SE to work with me on Sunday, but it had a flat tire. So I was stuck taking the Formula. Dad said he would have the tire fixed, and wanted the keys to the SE,  so he could take it out after the tire was fixed. I hesitated, and he asked me why. I just handed him the keys and didn't say anything. I get home from work last night, and he tells me the serp belt fell off the car. I took that meaning it fell off in the driveway, and said I would put a new one on Monday. Turns out he meant it fell off about 2 miles from home, and he drove it home after the belt fell off!!! I got kinda pissed, and said I would run a compression test, and see how much he fu##ed it up. Good news: cylinder 5 holds compression. Bad news: cylinders 1,2,3,4, and 6, all hold no comression, there is oil in what coolant is left, and I can hear the air escaping into the cooling system after I removed the cap and 'stat. I am now stuck with a non-running car, again. <P>Moral, life sucks! What do I do now? I can't keep an immobil car very long. That's why we have to sell off the ghia, and motorcycle. I might have to unload it to someone who feels like rebuilding an engine. I am so depressed, pissed off too!<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pffsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||9
Z||000001||TheFiero64||11-06-2000||11:13 AM||||I would be mad too. I never let anyone touch my Fieros for any reason<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||87ECO5||11-06-2000||11:14 AM||||[shaking my head in disbelief]<P>Unbelievable, pal!  I'm really sorry to hear this.||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||11-06-2000||11:17 AM||||56,<P>That's rough!  The way that I see it is that your old man has much more cash flow than you do, he is only a 50% partner in the ownership of the vehicle and he was at the wheel while the incident occured.  Unless I am missing something, he should at least be willing to take the blame and pay for half of a new engine (or similar agreement).  <P>That thing sounded strong too :~(  Come over when you have a chance.  Once I have my engine out of the 86, we can run it in yours until spring.  By then either I will have enough to start on the N* (yeah right) or you will have enough to swap out motors with a rebuilt one.  Don't you want to rebuild two motors this winter?  <P>William T. Thorn, III<P>||||reg||13
Z||000004||fiero56||11-06-2000||11:18 AM||||I just went out and looked at the trip meter. I put a total of 62 fun filled miles on it. Dad killed it in less than 12...<P>William, it was damn strong! I loved that car. Liked it even more than my pos Formula. It didn't handle like the Formula, yet, but I had plans for that car.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 11-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||lou_dias||11-06-2000||12:22 PM||||Shouldn't there have been enough valve clearance where the valves shouldn't have been damaged by the belt coming off.  And 86's didnt have a serpentine belt...||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||11-06-2000||12:29 PM||||The problem isn't with the timing chain. The engine ran when he parked it in the driveway, will probably still run.<P>The serpentine belt(not "v" belt), slipped off one of the pulleys. This means the water pump was then doing nothing, since it couldn't circulate the coolant. The 2 miles uphill to the house, overheated the engine, and either killed the head gaskets, warped heads/block, or cracked heads/block, or a combination. Don't know if I will even bother tearing it apart and finding out.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tigger||11-06-2000||12:35 PM||||Nope, I believe the serp belt does nothing for cam timing.  Basically it was a battery powered, air cooled VW/Fiero... Ouch!<P>I had a v-belt explode on mine, I drove it about 1/2 mile to get off the E-way and into a gas station, all the time watching my temp gauge.  I wouldn't want to go more than a mile without the belt.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||ChadMan||11-06-2000||12:41 PM||||Hey 56, that's heartbreaking.  My condolences on the passing of your 2.8.||||reg||9
